  (@custom "contractmetav0" (after data) "\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06cliver\00\00\00\00\00/27.0.0#5a7c5fe76530bf4248477ac812fc757146b98cc4\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bsource_repo\00\00\00\00\1dgithub:stellar-registry/perch\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06binver\00\00\00\00\00\050.3.5\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04name\00\00\00\12perch-doc-compiler\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\10scaffold_version\00\00\00\060.0.27\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bsource_repo\00\00\00\00)https://github.com/stellar-registry/perch\00\00\00")
  (@custom "contractspecv0" (after data) "\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\e6The document caps a compiler enforces, as [`PerchDocCompiler::limits`]\0areturns them. Versioned: a later budget (a complexity-weighted one, say)\0ais a new variant, which a consumer that does not know it refuses rather\0athan misreads.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09DocLimits\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\02V1\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0dFlatDocLimits\00\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00tWhere a compiled rule applies. `SelfAdmin` is account-agnostic: the\0aapplying account resolves it to its own address.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09RuleScope\00\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00<Calls to the applying account itself (`CallContract(self)`).\00\00\00\09SelfAdmin\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\17Calls to this contract.\00\00\00\00\08Contract\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\b1A cumulative spend cap lowered to OZ `spending_limit`'s install params\0a(`SpendingLimitAccountParams`). The tracked token is the rule's scope\0acontract, so it is not carried here.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bCompiledCap\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00!Rolling-window length in ledgers.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0eperiod_ledgers\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\002Cumulative amount ceiling over the rolling window.\00\00\00\00\00\0espending_limit\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\01\00\00\00EA compiled document: its canonical identity and the rules it becomes.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bCompiledDoc\00\00\00\00\05\00\00\00\9dThe canonical bytes `doc_hash` is the hash of. The account stores\0athem so anyone, including the recovery controller, can read back the\0afull applied document.\00\00\00\00\00\00\09canonical\00\00\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\b3`sha256(canonical bytes)` \e2\80\94 the hash the reviewer approved. Formatting\0aof the submitted JSON is irrelevant: a pretty-printed file and its\0aminified twin compile to the same hash.\00\00\00\00\08doc_hash\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\d2The fingerprint (`perch_recovery_interface::credential::Credential::\0afingerprint`) of every declared signer's credential, with external\0akeys canonicalized by their verifier. What revocation compares\0a(spec \c2\a78).\00\00\00\00\00\0cfingerprints\00\00\03\ea\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\01\03The compiled `recovery` member: zero or one entries (a `Vec` for the\0asame reason as [`CompiledRule::install`]). Present \e2\87\92 the document\0aenrolls account recovery, and the applier syncs this configuration to\0athe controller instance it names (`docs/recovery/`).\00\00\00\00\08recovery\00\00\03\ea\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\16CompiledRecoveryConfig\00\00\00\00\00<One compiled rule per document rule, in the submitted order.\00\00\00\05rules\00\00\00\00\00\03\ea\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0cCompiledRule\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\afOne rule, compiled to the exact shapes OZ's `add_context_rule` takes:\0aresolved addresses, OZ `Signer`s, and (for constrained rules) the\0ainterpreter program as `InstallParams`.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cCompiledRule\00\00\00\06\00\00\01\8eZero or one entries (a `Vec` for the same reason as `install`).\0aPresent \e2\87\92 also attach OZ `spending_limit` with these params \e2\80\94 the\0acumulative cap the stateless interpreter cannot express. The applier\0aresolves the policy's content-addressed address and keys it into the\0arule's policy map beside the interpreter; the tracked token is the\0arule's `Contract` scope (validation pins `token == scope`).\00\00\00\00\00\03cap\00\00\00\03\ea\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0bCompiledCap\00\00\00\00\eeThe interpreter program to attach: zero or one entries. A `Vec`\0abecause `#[contracttype]` has no conversion for `Option` of a custom\0astruct (`Option<u32>` on `valid_until` works because `u32` is a host\0atype). Empty \e2\87\92 a policy-free rule.\00\00\00\00\00\07install\00\00\00\03\ea\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0dInstallParams\00\00\00\00\00\00WThe rule's name in the document. The account matches installed rules\0aby name and scope.\00\00\00\00\04name\00\00\00\10\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05scope\00\00\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\09RuleScope\00\00\00\00\00\00PThe rule's signers, with external keys as declared (already\0averifier-canonical).\00\00\00\07signers\00\00\00\03\ea\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\06Signer\00\00\00\00\00{The last ledger the rule authorizes, if bounded: OZ's inclusive\0a`valid_until`, one below the document's `not-after-ledger`.\00\00\00\00\0bvalid_until\00\00\00\03\e8\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\00pWhat `derive_target` returns: the recovery target the controller binds\0ainto an attempt's statement (spec \c2\a77.1).\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0dDerivedTarget\00\00\00\00\00\00\05\00\00\00RThe target's canonical bytes: exactly what the completing `apply_doc`\0amust submit.\00\00\00\00\00\09canonical\00\00\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00hThe target's recovery `config_hash` (the current one, or the current\0aone with the declared ZK rotation).\00\00\00\0bconfig_hash\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\001`sha256` of `canonical`: the target's `doc_hash`.\00\00\00\00\00\00\08doc_hash\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00CFingerprints of every credential in the target (spec \c2\a77.3 rule 7).\00\00\00\00\0cfingerprints\00\00\03\ea\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\01GThe credentials occupying the replaced signer slots in the source:\0athe applied document's for lost-key, the baseline's for compromise.\0aExternal keys are canonicalized by their verifier, so a credential's\0a`fingerprint` is the one revocation compares. The controller records\0athem at T1 and the completion revokes them (spec \c2\a78).\00\00\00\00\08replaced\00\00\03\ea\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0aCredential\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00uFlat per-document caps: [`MAX_DOC_SIGNERS`], [`MAX_DOC_RULES`],\0a[`MAX_DOC_CANONICAL_BYTES`], [`MAX_RULE_NAME_BYTES`].\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0dFlatDocLimits\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\13max_canonical_bytes\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\13max_rule_name_bytes\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09max_rules\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bmax_signers\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\04\00\00\00dEverything `compile_doc` can refuse. (`#[scerr]` assigns sequential codes\0afrom 1, in variant order.)\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\10DocCompilerError\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00+The submitted document bytes are not UTF-8.\00\00\00\00\0aDocNotUtf8\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00lThe document failed fail-closed parsing (unknown field, bad shape, unsupported version, duplicate key, \e2\80\a6).\00\00\00\08DocParse\00\00\00\02\00\00\00sThe document failed semantic validation (dangling signer ref, malformed address or key, ambiguous empty list, \e2\80\a6).\00\00\00\00\0aDocInvalid\00\00\00\00\00\03\00\00\00CThe document names no network, or a network that is not this chain.\00\00\00\00\0cWrongNetwork\00\00\00\04\00\00\00AThe document cannot be lowered to rules (unsupported rule shape).\00\00\00\00\00\00\0aDocCompile\00\00\00\00\00\05\00\00\00\83The document exceeds a document cap ([`MAX_DOC_SIGNERS`], [`MAX_DOC_RULES`], [`MAX_DOC_CANONICAL_BYTES`], [`MAX_RULE_NAME_BYTES`]).\00\00\00\00\0bDocTooLarge\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\027A signer's external `key` is not its verifier-canonical form: either the verifier could not canonicalize it at all, or the declared bytes differ from the canonical form the verifier returns (e.g. a WebAuthn key carrying a credential-id suffix the verifier drops, or a non-canonical point encoding). The compiler refuses it rather than silently canonicalizing, so the bytes the document hash \e2\80\94 and a recovery attempt's `replacements_hash` \e2\80\94 bind are exactly the bytes the installed credential uses, and two signers cannot hide one physical key under two spellings.\00\00\00\00\15KeyNotCanonicalizable\00\00\00\00\00\00\07\00\00\00:`derive_target`: the current document enrolls no recovery.\00\00\00\00\00\0bNotEnrolled\00\00\00\00\08\00\00\00\fd`derive_target`: the replacement set breaks spec \c2\a77.3 rules 1-3 (not canonical, empty for lost-key, a signer id that is not replaceable or not declared in the source, or a change of credential kind or verifier), or the action is not a recovery attempt.\00\00\00\00\00\00\12ReplacementRefused\00\00\00\00\00\09\00\00\00y`derive_target`: the ZK enrollment is missing for a ZK mode, present for a guardian-only mode, or reuses the enrolled id.\00\00\00\00\00\00\14ZkEnrollmentMismatch\00\00\00\0a\00\00\00d`derive_target`: the target has no policy-free self-admin rule with a signer (the anti-brick check).\00\00\00\0cAdminLockout\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\01\00\00\00oThe canonical form and fragment hashes a compiler produces, as\0a[`PerchDocCompiler::capabilities`] returns them.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\14CompilerCapabilities\00\00\00\03\00\00\00=The CANON version `doc_hash` is `sha256` of (`CANONICAL.md`).\00\00\00\00\00\00\0dcanon_version\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00AThe domain tag of a recovery member's `config_hash` (spec \c2\a73.2).\00\00\00\00\00\00\0fconfig_hash_tag\00\00\00\00\10\00\00\004The domain tag of a rule's `rule_hash` (spec \c2\a73.2).\00\00\00\0drule_hash_tag\00\00\00\00\00\00\10\00\00\00\00\00\00\00CThe document caps every `compile_doc` and `derive_target` enforces.\00\00\00\00\06limits\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\09DocLimits\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\c7JSON bytes in \e2\86\92 compiled rules + canonical `doc_hash` out. Pure:\0ano auth, no storage. The document must name THIS network (its\0a`network` string must hash to the chain's network id), so a testnet\0adocument can never compile on mainnet or vice versa. It must also fit\0athe document caps ([`Self::limits`]), and every external signer key\0amust already be its verifier-canonical form: the compiler calls each\0anamed verifier's `batch_canonicalize_key` to check.\00\00\00\00\0bcompile_doc\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08doc_json\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0bCompiledDoc\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\10DocCompilerError\00\00\00\00\00\00\00KThe CANON version and the fragment hash domain tags this compiler\0aproduces.\00\00\00\00\0ccapabilities\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\14CompilerCapabilities\00\00\00\00\00\00\02#Derive a recovery target (`docs/recovery/spec.md` \c2\a77): `source_json`\0ais the account's applied document (lost-key) or the published\0abaseline (compromise); `current_json` is the applied document, whose\0arecovery member the target keeps. The target is the source with\0aexactly the declared replacements and ZK rotation, then validated,\0anetwork-bound, capped, compiled, and anti-brick-checked like any\0aapplied document. Pure: no auth, no storage. The controller calls it\0awhen an attempt begins, and completers simulate it to obtain the\0acanonical bytes.\00\00\00\00\0dderive_target\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bsource_json\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0ccurrent_json\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06action\00\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0eRecoveryAction\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0creplacements\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0eReplacementSet\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0dDerivedTarget\00\00\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\10DocCompilerError\00\00\00\02\00\00\00/One op of a postfix-encoded constraint program.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\02Op\00\00\00\00\00\10\00\00\00\01\00\00\000Pop `n` verdicts, push their Kleene conjunction.\00\00\00\03All\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\000Pop `n` verdicts, push their Kleene disjunction.\00\00\00\03Any\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00*Pop one verdict, push its Kleene negation.\00\00\00\00\00\03Not\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00)At least this many authenticated signers.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0aMinSigners\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\00)Invoked function is one of these symbols.\00\00\00\00\00\00\04FnIn\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\ea\00\00\00\11\00\00\00\01\00\00\00&Argument at index equals this address.\00\00\00\00\00\09ArgAddrEq\00\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\01\00\00\002Argument at index is the protected account itself.\00\00\00\00\00\0dArgAddrIsSelf\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\00%Argument at index equals this symbol.\00\00\00\00\00\00\08ArgSymEq\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\11\00\00\00\01\00\00\005Argument at index (a string) is one of these strings.\00\00\00\00\00\00\08ArgStrIn\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\04\00\00\03\ea\00\00\00\10\00\00\00\01\00\00\005Argument at index (a string) starts with this prefix.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cArgStrPrefix\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\10\00\00\00\01\00\00\00%Argument at index equals these bytes.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0aArgBytesEq\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\01\00\00\00#Argument at index equals this i128.\00\00\00\00\09ArgI128Eq\00\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\22Argument at index equals this u32.\00\00\00\00\00\08ArgU32Eq\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\00)The call has exactly this many arguments.\00\00\00\00\00\00\08ArgCount\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\00/Current ledger sequence is strictly below this.\00\00\00\00\0cLedgerBefore\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\00)Current ledger sequence is at least this.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0fLedgerAtOrAfter\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\00LA postfix-encoded constraint program. The last op produces the root\0averdict.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0aRpnProgram\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00!The ops, evaluated left to right.\00\00\00\00\00\00\03ops\00\00\00\03\ea\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\02Op\00\00\00\00\00<The wire-format version; only [`PROGRAM_VERSION`] validates.\00\00\00\07version\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\01UWhat the compiler stores in the interpreter for one `(account, rule)`: the\0aprogram plus the provenance hash of the rule it was compiled from. Sharing\0athis `#[contracttype]` between the compiler and the interpreter is what\0akeeps install params from ever being a hand-built `ScVal` \e2\80\94 both sides\0aencode and decode through exactly these types.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0dInstallParams\00\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\baThe source rule's `perch_ir::rule_hash`, not the whole document's\0ahash (the field keeps its original name). It binds the on-chain\0aprogram to the reviewed rule (provenance for lift/diff).\00\00\00\00\00\08doc_hash\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07program\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0aRpnProgram\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00NA signer credential, shaped like OZ `stellar_accounts::smart_account::Signer`.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0aCredential\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\01\00\00\00l`Signer::Delegated(address)`: a `G...` or `C...` address that\0aauthenticates through CAP-0071 delegated auth.\00\00\00\09Delegated\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\01\00\00\00H`Signer::External(verifier, key)`: a key checked by a verifier\0acontract.\00\00\00\08External\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\01\00\00\00lOne designated signer slot and the credential that replaces whatever\0athat slot holds in the source document.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bReplacement\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\008The credential the target document gives that signer id.\00\00\00\0acredential\00\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0aCredential\00\00\00\00\00CA document signer id listed in the enrolled `recovery.replaceable`.\00\00\00\00\09signer_id\00\00\00\00\00\00\10\00\00\00\01\00\00\01UA ZK enrollment a recovery completion installs.\0a\0aThe commitment is bound here, not only the id: completion runs under the\0azero-signer recovery rule, so nothing signs its arguments, and a\0acommitment supplied only at completion could be swapped by whoever\0asubmits the completing transaction first \e2\80\94 handing them the account's\0anext ZK factor.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cZkEnrollment\00\00\00\02\00\00\01\19The new leaf's inner commitment, `Poseidon2(DOM_LEAF, secret)`.\0aDerivation writes `id` and `commitment` into the target document's\0arecovery section, so the target hash binds them, and the completing\0a`apply_doc` inserts the leaf from the compiled target, never from a\0acall argument.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0acommitment\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00MThe new enrollment id. Must never have been enrolled for this\0aaccount before.\00\00\00\00\00\00\02id\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\01\00\00\00oEverything a `LostKey`/`Compromise` attempt changes about the source\0adocument. See `docs/recovery/spec.md` \c2\a77.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0eReplacementSet\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00uSigner replacements in strictly ascending `signer_id` byte order\0a(sorted, no duplicates) \e2\80\94 the one canonical order.\00\00\00\00\00\00\07signers\00\00\00\03\ea\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0bReplacement\00\00\00\01%The fresh ZK enrollment the completion installs, required exactly\0awhen the enrolled mode has a ZK factor (a ZK-evidenced completion\0aconsumes the enrolled credential, so it must install a fresh one).\0aEmpty or one entry \e2\80\94 a `Vec` because `#[contracttype]` cannot derive\0a`Option<CustomStruct>`.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0dzk_enrollment\00\00\00\00\00\03\ea\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0cZkEnrollment\00\00\00\02\00\00\00wWho may change the recovery configuration, and whether an authorized\0aattempt freezes ordinary activity (spec \c2\a72, \c2\a79).\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0fRecoveryProfile\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00wOwner authorization alone reconfigures; activity continues while an\0aattempt is authorized; the owner can always cancel.\00\00\00\00\04Loss\00\00\00\00\00\00\00iReconfiguration and upgrades also need the enrolled condition; an\0aauthorized attempt freezes the account.\00\00\00\00\00\00\09Protected\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\22The ZK factor (spec \c2\a73.1, \c2\a73.4).\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\10CompiledZkFactor\00\00\00\05\00\00\004The constructorless ZK adapter the controller calls.\00\00\00\07adapter\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00T`sha256` of the adapter's verification key; must equal the adapter's\0a`circuit_id()`.\00\00\00\0acircuit_id\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00rThe current credential's inner commitment, `Poseidon2(DOM_LEAF,\0asecret)`, from which the account inserts the leaf.\00\00\00\00\00\0acommitment\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00?The current credential's id, bound into its leaf and nullifier.\00\00\00\00\0denrollment_id\00\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00,The membership pool roots are accepted from.\00\00\00\04pool\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\14The guardian factor.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\13CompiledGuardianSet\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00@Guardian addresses (`G...` or `C...`), never the account itself.\00\00\00\09guardians\00\00\00\00\00\03\ea\00\00\00\13\00\00\00!`1 <= quorum <= guardians.len()`.\00\00\00\00\00\00\06quorum\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\02\00\00\00 Which factors a statement needs.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\14CompiledRecoveryMode\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\16A quorum of guardians.\00\00\00\00\00\0cGuardianOnly\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\13CompiledGuardianSet\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\0dOne ZK proof.\00\00\00\00\00\00\06ZkOnly\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\10CompiledZkFactor\00\00\00\01\00\00\00'A quorum of guardians and one ZK proof.\00\00\00\00\08Combined\00\00\00\02\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\13CompiledGuardianSet\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\10CompiledZkFactor\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\1dA compiled `recovery` member.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\16CompiledRecoveryConfig\00\00\00\00\00\09\00\00\00TThe enrolled baseline's canonical document hash, if compromise\0arecovery is enrolled.\00\00\00\08baseline\00\00\03\e8\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\d4[`config_hash`] of the canonical JSON of the recovery member, computed\0aby the doc compiler (spec \c2\a73.2). Configuration\0aidentity: two compiled configurations with the same `config_hash` are\0athe same configuration.\00\00\00\0bconfig_hash\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00 The adopted controller instance.\00\00\00\0acontroller\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00>Ledgers from an attempt's authorization until it can complete.\00\00\00\00\00\0ddelay_ledgers\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00gThe evidence window of a collecting attempt and the completion\0awindow of an authorized one, in ledgers.\00\00\00\00\0eexpiry_ledgers\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00DLifetime cap on evidence-based cancellations of authorized attempts.\00\00\00\0bmax_cancels\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\22The factors evidence must satisfy.\00\00\00\00\00\04mode\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\14CompiledRecoveryMode\00\00\00XWho may change the configuration, and whether an authorized attempt\0afreezes the account.\00\00\00\07profile\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0fRecoveryProfile\00\00\00\00{Signer ids (not credential fingerprints) a recovery may replace, so\0arotating a key does not change the configuration (#92).\00\00\00\00\0breplaceable\00\00\00\03\ea\00\00\00\10\00\00\00\03\00\00\01JThe action domain a statement authorizes. Evidence for one action never\0asatisfies another: the action code is the encoding's 26th byte and selects\0athe subject layout, so two statements that differ only in action have\0adifferent digests (and different encoded lengths for most pairs).\0a\0aThe numeric codes are part of the wire format.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0eRecoveryAction\00\00\00\00\00\05\00\00\00`Lost-key recovery: replace designated credentials in an agreed\0asnapshot of the current document.\00\00\00\07LostKey\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00YCompromise recovery: restore the enrolled baseline, with designated\0acredentials replaced.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0aCompromise\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\1eCancel one identified attempt.\00\00\00\00\00\06Cancel\00\00\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\83Change or remove the enrolled recovery configuration (the evidence a\0a`Protected` account needs in addition to owner authorization).\00\00\00\00\0bReconfigure\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00tApprove one scheduled account upgrade (the evidence a `Protected`\0aaccount needs in addition to owner authorization).\00\00\00\07Upgrade\00\00\00\00\05\00\00\00\02\00\00\00BRepresents different types of signers in the smart account system.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06Signer\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\01\00\00\00=A delegated signer that uses built-in signature verification.\00\00\00\00\00\00\09Delegated\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\01\00\00\00rAn external signer with custom verification logic.\0aContains the verifier contract address and the public key data.\00\00\00\00\00\08External\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\0e")
)
